WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.080
In a previous video, you could see us getting 
an old shipping container on our land.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.400
So, we built a big roof on top to make it rainproof.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.760
Added a storage system
on the outside for our material bank.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.200
And, a waste system on the other side.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.960
Now, we're going to finish it up in this last step,
 to add storage inside and store our garden tools.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.120
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.560
So, the container is here and it works great!

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.600
And, everything stays dry when it rains, 
and the wood is stored properly.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.454
The waste system functions!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.800
But, one thing, the most exciting part 
is actually the inside of the container.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.782
Which we're going to do right now,
because it's currently messy...

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.200
So, yeah, here we store a bunch of things,
because it's our most dry storage place.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.000
But, this also makes what we find in here very diverse.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.480
We have like saws, screws for the workspace,
and an old desk chair that someone gave to us...

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.040
And, I actually don't know why it's not in the office.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.880
This used to be 20 kilograms of cocoa powder,
and it's almost finished.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.000
It's been a few years that we've been working on that.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:15.680
Some tents, some racks from the refrigerator, 
a water pump for fires, linseed oil to coat our wood...

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.320
Chainsaw oil, incomplete Precious Plastic dome,
and a happy birthday sign.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:27.360
So, yeah, as you can see, a lot of random
objects with most of them useful.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.480
But, we need to organize this so we can
properly access them and store them.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:34.760
We're going to paint this side
and build a wall in the middle.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.055
So, this is going to be the clean area.

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:41.360
Where we're going to store things,
 like our food and long term storage, so it’s safe.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.839
Over here is going to be more the day
to day tools.

00:01:44.839 --> 00:01:48.920
And, the garden utilities we're all going to use,
so we can easily take them.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:53.280
So, at the end, this should all be a super nice, 
well equipped storage container.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.560
Just like the outside, the inside is pretty rough as well,
like rusty areas welded.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.160
And besides that, it's also just really dirty.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.040
So, it could use a good clean up.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.520
All right, so, first step:
take everything out and clean it up.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.560
Time to get started!

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.720
The container is now empty!

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.320
I actually didn't do anything.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.320
But next, we're gonna wash it.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:03.680
Right now, I'm going to start taking out
some loose pieces of paint.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.520
So, I'm going to start taking those out.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:12.840
Rust isn't that big of a deal,
because the paint we're using can paint over rust easily.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:18.800
So, yes, mainly just take all the loose paint out, 
so that the paint sticks to the container.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.120
The walls are now white, and it was a lot of work.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:22.360
Jaime spent a lot of time brushing everything,
to make sure it's all nice and white.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.640
It’s done!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:29.640
So, next, we’re going to build the wall inside to close it up.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:35.183
We have a lot of these panels from the yellow van I believe.

00:05:35.183 --> 00:05:37.746
In the end, they didn't reuse them.

00:05:37.746 --> 00:05:44.200
So, I'm going to reuse them now,
and make the part for the general help's workshop.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.520
They need like a tool part for all the tools, all the saws and scissors.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.760
I’m going to try to make it out of these. 

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:36.000
Let’s see, if it can take the nails.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.920
Yeah, I think it's strong enough!

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:59.760
So, I've been marking and drilling the holes to the board.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:07.840
But, I drilled one of the holes into the wrong place, 
so I have to make a plug there. 

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.040
So, meanwhile, Eemeli is working on the front part.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:15.040
I'm going to start here in the back,
to make the storage area.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.360
And, the first thing we're going to do
is close out this wall.

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.160
So, it separates the area,
and so the mice cannot get in here anymore.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.280
And, the tricky part is the bend in the container.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.280
So, here the beam is touching,
and the beam is straight.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.200
There is a big gap here.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:36.160
So, we need to try to make the wall snug here,
 so the mice cannot get through.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.360
The wall is now in, and it got a little bit darker here.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:12.760
But now, we're going to make the shelves inside.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.400
The container has an extra edge here.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.520
So, if you put the beam here, there's a gap.

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:26.080
So, we need to cut out a bit here..

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:15.360
All the shelves are now in, and it's getting pretty dark.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.800
It must be really annoying for you guys as well.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.687
But, luckily, the electronic parts arrived!

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:23.032
We're going to install the electricity!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:32.280
So, we have some cable, a socket and switch, two big LED lights, 
electrical boxes, cable connectors, some pipes...

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:34.920
And, tools.

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:38.640
We're going to install two lights,
two switches and a big socket here.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:40.668
So, we can charge all the batteries.

00:12:40.668 --> 00:12:46.400
We're going to hook it up to the solar system,
to make sure we get power supply.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.360
Electricity comes out from the ground here.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:56.293
We need to hook up the electricity to our main system.

00:12:56.293 --> 00:13:00.840
Which is set up here, and it should be relatively easy,
because we already have a fuse box in place.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:07.440
So, we’re just going to add it there,
and then continue to connect in the container.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.520
We have a pretty long light, 
and both of the connectors are at the end.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.360
But unfortunately, the ceiling is a bit bumpy.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.360
So, if we put this one here...

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.320
Without the connector, we cannot connect this one.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:46.280
And the other way around,
because there a big bump here.

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:49.640
So, I need to find out a logical place for this light...

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.960
Testing time!

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:02.560
Now, we can see things!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.960
So, now we just bought some off-the-shelf light switches.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:11.360
Which works, but we like to have them
from Precious Plastic.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:16.480
We already made sockets before,
but we would really like to have light switches as well.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:19.480
We made a few before testing,
but it didn't really work.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:20.640
And, then we stopped...

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:24.560
We got busy, so, for anyone that is able to make a mold...

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:28.640
To inject with a Precious Plastic machine,
you can get €1000.

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:31.960
For the first one, that shows us a working light switch.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.360
So, we need a table in the container for the general help.

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:48.320
And, we made a fancy drawing,
so we can start building it.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.040
And Robert is going to help me
with the metalworks.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.360
Cutting stuff and also welding.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:57.400
So, I can be doing other stuff...

00:15:58.520 --> 00:15:59.640
- Sounds good.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:03.920
Should come out fine, unless something goes wrong...

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:28.800
Chester is finally helping us.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.200
Thank you!

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:50.553
- Do you like it?

00:17:51.045 --> 00:17:52.725
Yes!

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:23.880
This is the tabletop.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:30.480
It's quite nice, actually, but the surface is very rough, so...

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:52.360
Linseed oil

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.160
It's heavier than I remember!

00:20:58.160 --> 00:20:59.400
- Look at them.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.920
So happy!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.160
Looks good!

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:22.080
Thank you.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:32.960
So, I'm going to start welding the holders 
for the brushcutters and the chainsaws.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.360
I'm going to use these off-cuts from the table.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.960
It's nice to use some offcuts,
since they're not going to waste.

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.760
Now, I got the things welded.

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:22.120
It sticks together.

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:27.240
I need to get something else,
to mount them to the container.

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:23.680
- Done?

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:24.551
Yeah, done!

00:23:24.551 --> 00:23:26.093
- Cool!

00:23:26.093 --> 00:23:27.760
Nice, Eemeli!

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:34.166
They look nice!

00:23:34.166 --> 00:23:35.640
Can I touch it?

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:36.140
- No!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:37.500
Okay...

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:38.646
- Did you finish Eemeli?

00:23:38.646 --> 00:23:40.071
Yeah!

00:23:41.757 --> 00:23:46.229
Now, all of the holders are painted,
so we can mount them to the wall.

00:23:46.229 --> 00:23:47.864
- Cool!

00:24:52.200 --> 00:24:54.720
Tools are here on the wall!

00:24:55.920 --> 00:24:59.476
Pretty nice how it turned out actually!

00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:05.141
- Are you speaking to yourself?

00:25:05.422 --> 00:25:07.241
Yes, mostly...

00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:18.080
So, this is the current mess that the general help uses.

00:25:19.200 --> 00:25:23.040
There’s these crates where all of this stuff is.

00:25:24.480 --> 00:25:28.560
Like, these helmets and the saws that are in the same one...

00:25:28.680 --> 00:25:32.280
And, the clothes are more or less
in the same crates...

00:25:34.253 --> 00:25:38.080
We also got some new tools, like these scissors.

00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:42.414
Rope!

00:25:43.960 --> 00:25:47.880
So, now we want to go through all of this stuff.

00:25:47.880 --> 00:25:52.080
To figure out what goes to the wall,
and what goes to the boxes.

00:25:56.800 --> 00:25:58.500
Nice glove!

00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:13.800
So, this is what went in the crates:

00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:17.520
Some brushcutter and chainsaw stuff.

00:26:21.240 --> 00:26:22.729
Handles.

00:26:24.360 --> 00:26:26.480
Blades.

00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:28.075
Rope.

00:26:32.160 --> 00:26:35.160
Gloves.

00:26:36.880 --> 00:26:39.880
And, the harnesses.

00:27:04.000 --> 00:27:12.960
Dave is working on the other side of the wall, 
so I’m only allowed to show this side of the container.

00:28:05.760 --> 00:28:07.120
- I'll be here listening.

00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:07.895
Huh?

00:28:07.895 --> 00:28:09.240
- I'll be here listening!

00:28:11.280 --> 00:28:17.840
The only thing left for me is to mount the vice!

00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:45.240
The vice is on the table, and the tools are on the wall.

00:28:45.760 --> 00:28:48.093
Everything is ready!

00:28:48.840 --> 00:28:52.800
And, there is still more space to add stuff.

00:28:54.600 --> 00:29:00.640
Another helmet, another axe, or more pliers or something...

00:29:01.400 --> 00:29:05.560
So, yeah, that's it for me!

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:14.280
For the last part, this is going to be a storage shelf for the kitchen.

00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:16.763
We’re going to use this coated plywood.

00:29:17.520 --> 00:29:20.400
The main reason for using this is that it's easy to clean.

00:29:20.400 --> 00:29:22.680
Because, this side is going to be for the kitchen.

00:29:22.680 --> 00:29:26.280
And, they might have experiments with
fermentation or some leaking jars.

00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:29.280
So, in this way we can easily wipe it clean.

00:29:29.680 --> 00:29:35.440
Not a big fan of using this material, 
but we didn't really find another option that has big large panels.

00:29:35.440 --> 00:29:38.847
So, if you have suggestions for that 
for us in the future, let us know!

00:29:38.847 --> 00:29:44.640
The design is pretty much based on a standard plywood size,
which you find here and then it's chopped in half.

00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:48.000
So, that will be the width of this whole shelving system.

00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:52.320
Which makes it easy to build,
but also easy to take apart later on.

00:29:52.320 --> 00:29:54.080
Because, we didn't have to cut it that much.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:57.560
Time to get started building!

00:29:57.560 --> 00:29:59.200
Let’s make some space!

00:30:25.080 --> 00:30:31.680
There is a big dent, which might be hard to see, but I see it...

00:30:32.280 --> 00:30:36.000
The height of the shelf is based on 
some storage items we have.

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:39.280
So, we have these ones,
which we already use in the kitchen right now.

00:30:40.160 --> 00:30:43.240
But, we also have them in a bigger version.

00:30:43.320 --> 00:30:48.000
Then, we have a jerrycan size, which is how
we get our vinegar and things like that.

00:30:48.280 --> 00:30:52.160
A classic jar size, which will be one shelf 
with exactly two on top.

00:30:52.680 --> 00:30:56.920
So, we can reuse them to store things,
and preserve them for the long term.

00:31:16.480 --> 00:31:18.972
All the wood has been cut and drilled!

00:31:18.972 --> 00:31:20.440
Now, it's time for assembly!

00:31:20.600 --> 00:31:22.130
This is the fun part.

00:31:22.130 --> 00:31:23.715
Eemeli is going to help here.

00:31:27.416 --> 00:31:28.526
- Yes!

00:31:30.879 --> 00:31:32.031
Finnish precision.

00:31:32.360 --> 00:31:34.560
So, there should be space here in the back...

00:32:14.920 --> 00:32:17.160
Everything is now built!

00:32:17.160 --> 00:32:23.160
We just need to clean it up,
and then let the teams fill up in the storage areas!

00:33:57.000 --> 00:33:58.360
All right, so, the container is ready!

00:33:58.360 --> 00:33:59.640
Let me show you the inside!

00:33:59.640 --> 00:34:00.720
It's a bit tight in there...

00:34:00.720 --> 00:34:03.720
So, we need a GoPro.

00:34:10.080 --> 00:34:13.080
So, on this side, we have all the garden tools.

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:16.320
Hanging and organized by category of tools.

00:34:16.800 --> 00:34:19.800
It's easy at the end of the day
to see what is missing.

00:34:20.040 --> 00:34:25.920
So, we can either find it back on the land, 
and make sure everything is in stock.

00:34:25.920 --> 00:34:27.943
In here, we have our brush cutters.

00:34:27.943 --> 00:34:32.560
We have two electric ones and one gas-powered,
so we can easily take them out.

00:34:33.600 --> 00:34:37.360
Underneath, we have the chainsaws, 
with an electric one and gas powered as well.

00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:42.600
Then, on this side, we have all the smaller tools that we use.

00:34:44.085 --> 00:34:49.000
So, we have some hammers, protective helmets, saws...

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:51.321
Well, you can see all the things.

00:34:51.321 --> 00:34:57.000
Here, we can charge the batteries 
for the chainsaw and the brush cutter.

00:34:59.400 --> 00:35:03.000
We have a vice to put in a chainsaw,
so we can sharpen it.

00:35:03.320 --> 00:35:05.446
So, we got some sharpening tools.

00:35:05.446 --> 00:35:07.978
We have some organic rope, 
so if you want to tie something quickly...

00:35:07.978 --> 00:35:11.640
We get that, to put it on the land, and then just rots away.

00:35:12.080 --> 00:35:13.840
So, no plastic rope.

00:35:13.840 --> 00:35:17.600
Gloves, with right and the left one separated, since it’s easier.

00:35:17.600 --> 00:35:20.235
And below, we have all the oils and gasoline.

00:35:20.235 --> 00:35:24.080
For the chainsaw and the brush cutters,
to make sure they can run.

00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:30.960
So, these are all the garden tools in here, 
and sort of the landscape area.

00:35:31.080 --> 00:35:32.040
And, over here...

00:35:33.120 --> 00:35:35.280
We have this storage area.

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:40.440
So, on this side, the workspace.

00:35:40.756 --> 00:35:43.756
Here, we have things like cutting disks...

00:35:44.160 --> 00:35:46.960
Drills in stock...

00:35:46.960 --> 00:35:49.960
And, drill bits.

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:52.880
The screws from our screw system...

00:35:52.880 --> 00:35:55.880
Water filters, like a whole year supply of them.

00:35:56.040 --> 00:35:58.759
To make sure we have clean drinking water.

00:35:59.743 --> 00:36:04.360
We also store linseed oil and we have some paints here.

00:36:04.520 --> 00:36:07.520
Some electrical components...

00:36:07.920 --> 00:36:10.160
Yeah, it's not really fully equipped yet.

00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:15.360
We can now start ordering all the things,
so until that time, it will be a bit empty.

00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:21.480
We can also use it to store some future projects 
that are coming up, like this one.

00:36:21.760 --> 00:36:24.080
But, that’s the workspace area!

00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:28.920
Then, over here we have the kitchen, 
where we store things like bulk foods.

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:30.600
So, in these containers, for instance...

00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:34.120
This one has rice.

00:36:34.120 --> 00:36:37.120
If you're from Portugal, you know this guy: tremoços (= lupin beans).

00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:38.800
Good snack!

00:36:38.800 --> 00:36:41.800
We also use it to store preserved food here.

00:36:43.240 --> 00:36:44.880
Over here, we have crates.

00:36:44.880 --> 00:36:47.680
They all fit the standardized crate.

00:36:47.680 --> 00:36:50.680
Some bottles to preserve the food.

00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:54.160
Things like brushes and cloths to clean.

00:36:54.160 --> 00:36:55.200
These are all new ones.

00:36:55.200 --> 00:36:58.880
So, when they wear out or they break,
we can stock ourselves up with this.

00:36:59.960 --> 00:37:02.960
Some potatoes.

00:37:03.000 --> 00:37:06.463
And here, there is also a bit more kitchen things.

00:37:06.463 --> 00:37:10.700
But, less food based, so baking soda for instance to clean

00:37:10.700 --> 00:37:16.258
Our toilet paper, a big container of liquid soap,
 to refill our hand soap.

00:37:16.258 --> 00:37:18.400
So, we didn't have to buy the small packages all the time...

00:37:19.040 --> 00:37:21.720
Washing powder.

00:37:21.720 --> 00:37:26.040
And, that's kind of the main point of having this container,
so that we can buy things in bulk.

00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:31.409
Because, buying things in bulk means
 we can find a really good supplier.

00:37:32.006 --> 00:37:34.104
We really put a lot of effort into that!

00:37:34.104 --> 00:37:36.600
Less transport and less packaging!

00:37:36.960 --> 00:37:43.480
And also, just less work, like less receipts, 
less administration is just simplifying life.

00:37:43.760 --> 00:37:47.280
And, up until now it was kind of hard to do,
because we didn't have the storage place.

00:37:47.280 --> 00:37:54.080
But now, we can really bulk up, and make sure
 we make better choices in the things we buy!

00:38:00.840 --> 00:38:03.360
All right, so, now the container is fully renovated!

00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:05.200
This is part of a three series video.

00:38:05.200 --> 00:38:07.920
The first one, where we built the roof on top.

